UNREAL ENGINE IS NOT INCLUDED IN THIS REPOSITORY
================================================

Gem Hunter is built with Unreal Engine, but Unreal Engine is NOT part of this
repository and is NOT covered by any licence in it.

Unreal Engine is licensed by Epic Games, Inc. under the Unreal Engine End User
Licence Agreement, which is not an open-source licence:

    https://www.unrealengine.com/eula

What this means in practice:

  * No engine source, binaries or engine Content are committed here. The
    .gitignore enforces the generated-file side of that; the rest is on us.
  * To build Gem Hunter you need your own Epic Games account and your own
    installation of Unreal Engine, and you accept Epic's EULA directly with Epic.
  * Our Apache-2.0 grant covers our code only. It grants you nothing with respect
    to Unreal Engine.
  * Anything you redistribute that contains Unreal Engine code or content is
    governed by Epic's EULA, not by ours.

Project files that reference the engine (GemHunter.uproject, the .Build.cs and
.Target.cs files) are ours and are Apache-2.0. The engine they point at is Epic's.


THIRD-PARTY PLUGINS
===================

The core game must stay buildable by anyone who clones the repository, so it
depends only on plugins that ship with Unreal Engine or are redistributable under
an open-source licence.

  * Enabled, engine-bundled: PCG, ModelingToolsEditorMode. Covered by Epic's EULA.
  * No paid or Fab-marketplace plugin may become a core dependency. Marketplace
    content is generally non-redistributable, so a contributor could not build the
    game. Such plugins stay optional, or stay out.
  * Diggable terrain is deliberately behind the IDiggableTerrain interface
    (Source/GemHunterCore/Public/DiggableTerrain.h) so the backend can be swapped
    without touching gameplay. The candidates have different licence profiles:
    UE5VoxelTerrainDemo is open source, Voxel Plugin 2 is paid. Nothing is chosen
    yet, and nothing is vendored here.
  * Cesium for Unreal (Apache-2.0) is a possible optional dependency for a real
    globe. Its default terrain stream, Cesium ion, is a separate hosted service,
    so it must stay optional for an open-source build.


DATA SOURCES
============

  * U.S. Geological Survey, Mineral Resources Data System (MRDS). U.S. Government
    work, no use restrictions. https://mrdata.usgs.gov/mrds/
  * Smithsonian Open Access. CC0 for open-access items, but the NMNH Geogallery
    listing mixes CC0 with "usage conditions apply", so each item is checked
    individually before use. https://www.si.edu/openaccess
  * Mindat. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, quarantined in data/mindat/ with its own LICENSE.
    https://www.mindat.org/
  * GIA Gems & Gemology and other gemmological literature are used as design
    reference only. Codex text is written in our own words; no copyrighted text
    is reproduced in the game data.
